== the numbered list prints every entry ==
    1  echo one
    2  ls
    3  cd /tmp
    4  git status
== a trailing count prints only the most recent entries ==
    3  cd /tmp
    4  git status
== a non-numeric count is rejected without printing the list ==
1:9: error: Builtin `history`: 'foo' is not a valid count.
     1 |  history foo; echo "rc=$?"
       |          ^~~
rc=2
== a count past the list size still prints every entry, no overflow ==
    1  echo one
    2  ls
    3  cd /tmp
    4  git status
== the print flag echoes its operands and stores nothing ==
alpha
beta
== builtin history -a no longer reports an unknown builtin ==
continued
== type reports the builtin ==
history is a shell builtin
== clear empties the list ==
cleared
== history -r <file> merges the named file into the list:
    1  existing one
    2  existing two
    3  merged alpha
    4  merged beta
== history -r on a missing file errors:
rc=1
recall ok
fc replacement ok
search casefold ok
history expansion ok
history words ok
history modifiers ok
history filtering ok
cmdhist and lithist ok
histappend ok
history option ok
ignoreeof ok
